  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.4.10 (forks 2.4.9) - FIXED (CUDA at O2, the 5.4.9 default): kernels could compute wrong results because branches that differ between the threads of a warp were emitted bra.uni (the uniform analysis counted loop-counter phis, atomic results and loads as uniform). Upgrade from 5.4.9 if you use CUDA. See CHANGELOG.md. v5.4.9 (forks 2.4.8) - BEHAVIOR CHANGE: the default optimization level is O2 (was O1): the full suite passes, compile time is about the same (ptxas faster), CUDA kernels can be much faster (BC7 encode +31 %); builder.Release() restores O1. FIXED: two O2 bugs (a shared-memory load moved below a barrier, a race on CUDA / OpenCL / Velocity; OpenCL Half kernels failed to build); Wasm: a memset between launches is ordered after the kernels before it; WebGL: ulong compares are unsigned; every backend: a bool folded to a constant can be turned into an int; WebGPU: a workaround for an NVIDIA D3D12 driver miscompile of stores into local arrays, plain access of a buffer also used with atomics compiles; OpenCL barriers fence local memory. See CHANGELOG.md. v5.4.4 (forks 2.4.4) - FIXED (CUDA): kernels failed to load on drivers whose PTX JIT is older than the CUDA version they report (the ISA is now probed). NEW (CUDA): Half works on GPUs below sm_53, emulated through f32 with one rounding (fma exact); native devices unchanged. FIXED (WebGPU): three shader-creation failures (atomic buffers read plainly across blocks, elements of a byte sub-view, struct variables), and byte ranges not 4-byte aligned were dropped or overwrote neighbouring bytes on readback, upload, device copy and fill. See CHANGELOG.md. v5.4.3 (forks 2.4.3) - FIXED: a nested threshold ternary such as `v >= 40 ? 2 : (v >= 15 ? 1 : 0)` gave the wrong value (1 instead of 2) on CUDA, OpenCL, WebGPU, WebGL, Wasm and Velocity: the SSA builder typed a stack value that merges a comparison with an integer as a bool. FIXED (WebGPU): a while (true) loop whose body starts with an if/else hung the GPU (DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_HUNG). FIXED (WebGPU): SubView of a view parameter failed shader validation; (Wasm) SubView wrote to address 0; (WebGPU) a barrier loop whose exit depends on a buffer load was rejected. CUDA load failures now carry the driver JIT log. See CHANGELOG.md. v5.4.2 (forks 2.4.2) - FIXED: weights streamed into an OpenCL buffer (CopyFromStreamAsync, InferenceSession.CreateFromStreamAsync) could arrive with later chunks' data in earlier places on a driver that reads host memory late (confirmed on an AMD RX 590, where SD-Turbo produced noise); the upload now pins its chunk and waits for each chunk's copy. See CHANGELOG.md. v5.4.1 (forks 2.4.1) - WebGPU, WebGL and Wasm drop the debug assertions before code generation, so the dead index/length compare chains of every ArrayView access are no longer emitted (TRELLIS.2 GEMM WGSL 592 KB -> 331 KB, cold first launch 6.6 s -> 1.25 s), and WebGPU loads each scalar slot once at kernel entry (fixes a DXC E_FAIL phi of resource handles; attention -11 %). See CHANGELOG.md. v5.4.0 (forks 2.4.0) - Velocity, the SIMD CPU backend, is a complete backend and the default CPU backend: AllAccelerators() / AllAcceleratorsAsync() register it instead of the plain CPU accelerator on desktop and server (BEHAVIOR CHANGE: the plain CPU accelerator is the debugging backend now, register it with builder.DefaultCPU(); 32-bit processes keep it, the browser registers no CPU accelerator). Velocity runs all 731 shared tests: Half, BFloat16, FP8, FP4 and packed 4-bit types, 1D/2D/3D grids and groups, groups of up to 256 threads with fast barriers, Vector256 / Vector512 device types. MathF.Truncate / Math.Truncate work on every compiled backend. See CHANGELOG.md. v5.3.9 (forks 2.3.14) - FIXED: a loop with a compile-time trip count inside an if, whose result is used after the if, returned the value from before the loop in every thread that took the branch, on CUDA, OpenCL, WebGPU, WebGL and Wasm (LoopUnrolling left the exit block phi naming the cleared loop header as its source). See CHANGELOG.md.",
